  "body": "Reported by the maintainer in chat, 2026-11-16.\n\nWhat happens: a 2D Adaptive operation has a selected face. The containment is set to outside. Generate fails:\n\n```\ngenerate failed: could not generate the toolpath: 2D Adaptive1: invalid machining parameters: adaptive: the center area has no room for an entry\n```\n\nExpected: with outside containment the tool can start outside the selected area, in open air or at the stock side. The entry does not need room in the centre of the area. The operation generates a toolpath, or it gives a refusal that names the control to change.\n\nEvidence:\n\n- Project: `testdata/models/fig8.camproj` (model `fig8.step`), 2D Adaptive, tool `EM-0800-4FL` (8 mm end mill), build `v0.22.0`.\n- The message comes from the entry search of the Adaptive planner. It looks for a helix or plunge position inside the area.\n\nTo find:\n\n1. Which entry positions the planner tries when the containment is outside.\n2. If the planner reads the containment before it searches for an entry.\n3. If an entry from outside the stock is available to the planner for this case.\n\nSafety: a fix changes the entry moves, thus the posted G-code. The verify check and the post gate must stay unchanged. An entry from outside must not go through a fixture or uncut stock.\n\nDone means: a test selects a face with outside containment on a part of this shape. The operation generates and verifies clean, or the refusal names the control that the user must change. The message \"no room for an entry\" does not appear for a tool that can enter from the open side.\n",
